# Kingdom: Project Rules

## Stack
- Vite + TypeScript + Phaser 3
- Browser game, no backend
- Run: `npm run dev`
- Deploys to GitHub Pages on push to main (.github/workflows/deploy.yml)

## Structure (do not explore to confirm this, trust it)
- src/main.ts: Phaser game config and boot (loads MapScene)
- src/world/: game data and logic only, no Phaser imports
  - tile.ts: Tile type (terrain, owner, city, improvement, road), terrain rules, yields, claim costs
  - map.ts: WorldMap, map generation, neighbors, raiseHeight/lowerHeight
  - units.ts: unit types/stats (builder, settler), training, builder jobs, movement costs, reachable()
  - game.ts: GameState: players, gold/food/stone, turns, claim, recruit/train/move/jobs, settlers founding cities, win checks, rival AI
  - save.ts: autosave/load to localStorage (key kingdom-save-v3)
- src/scenes/: rendering and input only
  - MapScene.ts: draws hexes, roads, buildings, units, borders; selection, movement, modes, camera; autosaves after every redraw
  - Hud.ts: DOM overlay (collapsible stats/help/selection panels, mode bar, tooltip, game over)
  - Menu.ts: start screen (map size, rivals, free building, continue)
- src/game/ and the other files in src/scenes/ are old unused stubs

## Behavior rules
- Do NOT run ls, find, or read files to explore the project unless I ask or a file I mention is missing.
- Only touch files related to the current request.
- Do one step at a time. Do not add features I didn't ask for.
- Do not plan the full implementation in your head first. Write the files, then fix issues.
- Keep world logic out of scenes. Scenes read from world, never the other way around.
- Scenes change the world only through GameState methods (perform, recruit, moveUnit, doJob, foundCity, endTurn).
- If you add new state to GameState, Tile or Unit, add it to save.ts too.
- After changes, tell me what changed in 1-3 lines and how to test it.

## Game rules (current)
- Pointy-top hexes, odd rows shifted right (odd-r offset). Sizes: small 20x14, medium 30x20, large 44x30, huge 60x40
- Height 0-5: 0 water, 1 sand, 2-3 grass, 4 hills, 5 mountain
- Players: You (blue) + 0-3 AI rivals. 0 rivals = sandbox (no win conditions)
- Gold per turn: tile yield (sand/grass 1, hills 2, mountain 0) + city 3 + capital 5
- Food is supply: capital 3, city 2, farm 3. Units (and units in training) use food: builder 1, settler 2
- Stone: mines give 2/turn (will pay for walls)
- Builder (15g, instant, 2 moves): one job per turn on own land: farm (grass/sand, 5g), mine (hills/mountain, 8g), road (2g), raise/lower its tile or a neighbor (3g)
- Settler (10g + 10g per city owned, 3 turns to train, 2 moves): founds a city on unclaimed or own land, 3+ hexes from any city; settler is consumed. One unit in training per city
- Move costs: grass/sand 1, hills 2, mountain 3, road-to-road 0.5. Full-move units can always step 1 tile
- Claim: buy unowned land bordering yours, within 4 hexes of one of your cities. Price +8% per tile bought
- Owned land can never be claimed; only conquering the city (step 3) takes it
- Win: take every rival capital or hold 60% of land

## Roadmap
1. DONE builders, food, stone, farms, mines, roads, settlers
2. City HP + walls (builders build walls with stone)
3. Troops: swordsman, archer, knight; combat; capture cities by destroying them; captured city takes the land closest to it
4. AI uses builders and troops (AI already uses settlers)
5. Balance pass
